				564,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore missing closing parentheses in codegen entry point\n\nThe prior `)` → `;` bulk statement-termination refactor stripped closing parentheses from 8 call expressions in the standalone codegen entry point (`Main.ts` scoped to `Codegen.ts`), leaving malformed syntax across `resolve`, `RunExtHostCodegen`, `console.error`, `process.exit`, `console.log`, and the `void Main()` invocation.\n\nRestore `)` before `;` in all affected expressions and close the outer `resolve(Cwd, ...)` call. The entry point now compiles with balanced parentheses and valid TypeScript statement syntax, matching the same fix pattern applied across other Cocoon modules.",
			"SHA": "316a700e3ec25fe4acbff4b2f03056773d927641"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-13T02:39:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				564,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore missing closing parenthesis in codegen schema formatter\n\nThe prior `)` → `;` bulk statement-termination refactor stripped the closing `)` from the `.join()` call in `FormatDocComment`, leaving a malformed chained method expression in the codegen emit schema.\n\nAdd the missing `)` before `;` to restore valid TypeScript syntax for the array join expression that builds JSDoc body lines. This is a pure syntax fix with no behavioral change.",
			"SHA": "67ac5bd1d6decfd4dbf32da80cbb1d08423dc377"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-13T02:39:19Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				564,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore missing closing parentheses in config files\n\nTwo files were left with unbalanced parentheses after the prior bulk statement-termination refactor stripped `)` from call expressions. Restore the missing closing parenthesis: `console.log(_Error;` → `console.log(_Error);` in ESBuild Base config, and `parseInt(process.env.MOUNTAIN_PORT, 10;` → `parseInt(process.env.MOUNTAIN_PORT, 10);` in Mountain config resolver.\n\nBoth files now compile with valid syntax and balanced parentheses.",
			"SHA": "f3e8ae39da065d1354e4cb6852de82cf8802b5e9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-13T02:38:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				564,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore missing closing parentheses in WebSocket Server.ts\n\nThe prior `)` → `;` bulk statement-termination refactor from the Effect-TS removal erroneously stripped the closing `)` and opening `(` from 30+ call expressions and constructor invocations in `Source/Bootstrap/WebSocket/Server.ts`, leaving malformed syntax across the auth matching, request handling, upgrade flow, and server lifecycle.\n\nRestore all missing `)` and `(` tokens in `Buffer.from`, `timingSafeEqual`, `RouteRequest` (3 call sites), `ws.send`, `JSON.stringify` (2 call sites), `import(\"ws\")`, `createServer`, `WebSocketServer`, `sock.write`, `sock.destroy`, `wss.handleUpgrade`, `CocoonDevLog` (3 call sites), `ws.on` (4 call sites), `res` (2 call sites), `process.stdout.write`, `rej`, and the `http.on(\"upgrade\", ...)` arrow closure closing boundary.\n\nAll expressions now compile with balanced parentheses and valid statement syntax — identical to the fix pattern applied in `Main.ts`.",
			"SHA": "e37458a20ddd9da5a44290771820d5baf4cc47b6"
		}
